From bceea40ca0f3559fca7843b0b3d0b9c2b440c036 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 23:12:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/30] util/os_misc: include <unistd.h> where sysconf is the
 answer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The include block at the top of os_misc.c is a chain of platform names
ending in "#error unexpected platform in os_sysinfo.c". It fires before
any of the three implementations below is even looked at, so a platform
that has sysconf() — which all three prefer, each testing HAVE_SYSCONF
in its first branch — still could not compile the file.

Add <unistd.h> under HAVE_SYSCONF as the last branch. That is all such
a platform needs from this block, and it removes the reason to keep
adding an OS name here whenever one appears.

Additive: it is an #elif at the end of the chain, unreachable for every
platform that already matched, and the #error stays for a platform with
neither a listed OS nor sysconf.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 3 item 6 (physical memory / page size queries)
Why: Horizon reaches none of the listed platforms. sysconf itself is
  supplied by this project's compat/ — devkitA64's newlib declares it
  (sys/unistd.h:236) and defines every _SC_ name used here, but never
  defines the symbol — so HAVE_SYSCONF is true and the three functions
  below work unchanged; only this block stood in the way.
Evidence: building src/util for aarch64/horizon fails with
    os_misc.c:81:2:  #error unexpected platform in os_sysinfo.c
    os_misc.c:407:2: #error unexpected platform in os_misc.c
    os_misc.c:507:2: #error unexpected platform in os_sysinfo.c
  With compat/ linked, configure reports
    Checking for function "sysconf" : YES
  and only the first of the three remained.
Upstream: yes — it is additive and cannot change any platform that
  compiles today.
---
 src/util/os_misc.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util/os_misc.c b/src/util/os_misc.c
index ee2b790..0ef5128 100644
--- a/src/util/os_misc.c
+++ b/src/util/os_misc.c
@@ -77,6 +77,11 @@
 #elif DETECT_OS_FUCHSIA
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <zircon/syscalls.h>
+#elif HAVE_SYSCONF
+/* Reached only when none of the platforms above matched. Every
+ * implementation below has a sysconf() path and takes it first, so
+ * <unistd.h> is all such a platform needs — no new branch per OS. */
+#include <unistd.h>
 #else
 #error unexpected platform in os_sysinfo.c
 #endif
